---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import LifecycleNotice from "../../components/StandardLifecycleNotice.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/japangaap/asbj38.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.summary}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope — Consolidation-Specific Interim Mechanics" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Why Consolidated Interim Reporting Needs Its Own Guidance" },
        { id: "s4", label: "Subsidiary Interim Data Alignment" },
        { id: "s5", label: "Coordination With ASBJ Statement No. 37" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Worked Example — Consolidating Subsidiary Interim Data" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Critical Judgments & Estimates" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Relationship to IAS/IFRS" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Glossary" },
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>

  <LifecycleNotice
    type="active"
    explanation="RECENCY NOTE: Issued October 16, 2025 alongside ASBJ Statement No. 37 (Interim Financial Reporting), No. 39, and No. 40 — details should be cross-checked against ASBJ's current published materials."
    link=""
    linkText=""
  />

  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-header" id="s1">
      <span class="num">1</span>
      <h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Consolidation-specific mechanics for interim reporting purposes</div>
        <div class="principle">ASBJ Statement No. 38 addresses SPECIFIC procedural questions that arise when PREPARING CONSOLIDATED interim (semi-annual) financial statements — going BEYOND the GENERAL interim reporting principles set out in ASBJ Statement No. 37 (see the companion poster) to address the ADDITIONAL complexity of combining a GROUP of entities' interim-period data.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s2">
      <span class="num">2</span>
      <h2>Scope — Consolidation-Specific Interim Mechanics</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2">
        <div class="ctitle cw">Groups preparing consolidated interim financial statements</div>
        <div class="principle">This Statement applies to PARENT companies preparing CONSOLIDATED interim financial statements, addressing PROCEDURAL questions SPECIFIC to combining subsidiaries' interim-period financial data WITHIN the group's own interim report.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s3">
      <span class="num">3</span>
      <h2>Why Consolidated Interim Reporting Needs Its Own Guidance</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Consolidation adds genuine procedural complexity beyond standalone interim reporting</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">
          <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">PREPARING a SINGLE entity's OWN interim report is RELATIVELY straightforward — condense the statements, apply CONSISTENT policies, assess MATERIALITY for the shorter period. CONSOLIDATING a GROUP's interim figures adds GENUINE additional complexity: SUBSIDIARIES may have their OWN interim reporting cycles, intercompany ELIMINATIONS must still be performed at the INTERIM date, and NON-CONTROLLING INTERESTS must still be correctly ALLOCATED — all WITHIN the CONDENSED, time-pressured context of interim reporting. This Statement provides the SPECIFIC procedural guidance addressing THESE consolidation-specific questions.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s4">
      <span class="num">4</span>
      <h2>Subsidiary Interim Data Alignment</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2">
        <div class="ctitle cs">Ensuring subsidiary data is genuinely comparable at the interim date</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">
          <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">CONSISTENT with the GENERAL fiscal year-end alignment principle established under ASBJ Statement No. 22 (Consolidated Financial Statements — see the companion poster), this Statement addresses HOW subsidiaries' OWN interim-period data should be ALIGNED and INCORPORATED into the GROUP's consolidated interim figures, ensuring genuinely COMPARABLE, CONSISTENT information across the CONSOLIDATED group at the interim reporting date.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s5">
      <span class="num">5</span>
      <h2>Coordination With ASBJ Statement No. 37</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2">
        <div class="ctitle cw">A companion piece within the broader reform package</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">
          <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">This Statement was issued ON THE SAME DATE as ASBJ Statement No. 37 (renaming the general framework from "Semi-annual" to "Interim" Financial Reporting), No. 39 (consolidated cash flow statement amendments), and No. 40 (tax effect accounting amendments) — TOGETHER forming a genuinely COORDINATED reform package addressing DIFFERENT facets of the SAME underlying interim reporting transition.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s6">
      <span class="num">6</span>
      <h2>Worked Example — Consolidating Subsidiary Interim Data</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2">
        <div class="ctitle cw">Aligning a subsidiary's interim figures with the parent's reporting date</div>
        <div class="worked worked--flush">
          <div class="wk-title">Example: A domestic subsidiary's interim consolidation</div>
          <div class="wk-body">A parent company preparing its consolidated interim report needs to incorporate a wholly-owned domestic subsidiary's own interim-period results, with intercompany sales during the period requiring elimination.</div>
          <div class="wk-answer">The parent INCORPORATES the subsidiary's interim data, ELIMINATING intercompany sales and any UNREALISED profit remaining in inventory at the interim date — CONSISTENT with the same GENERAL consolidation principles applied ANNUALLY (per ASBJ Statement No. 22), but APPLIED within the CONDENSED, interim reporting timeframe this Statement addresses.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s7">
      <span class="num">7</span>
      <h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">What ASBJ Statement No. 38 requires</div>
        <div class="check-list">
          <span>Scope of consolidation for interim reporting purposes</span>
          <span>Basis for aligning subsidiary interim-period data with the group's reporting date</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s8">
      <span class="num">8</span>
      <h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
        <div class="two-col">
          <div>
            <div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div>
            <div class="dot-list">
              <span>Appropriate alignment of subsidiary interim-period data with the parent's reporting date</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div>
            <div class="dot-list">
              <span>Interim-period intercompany elimination estimates where precise data is not yet finalised</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s9">
      <span class="num">9</span>
      <h2>Relationship to IAS/IFRS</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">A procedural refinement, not a substantive divergence point</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">
          <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">IAS 34 addresses consolidated interim reporting through the SAME general principles applied to standalone interim reporting, WITHOUT a SEPARATE, dedicated standard for consolidation-specific interim mechanics — J-GAAP's CHOICE to address this through a DEDICATED companion Statement reflects its GENERAL preference for detailed, PRACTICAL procedural guidance, RATHER than a substantive divergence in the UNDERLYING consolidation principles themselves.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s10">
      <span class="num">10</span>
      <h2>Statement Mapping</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2">
        <div class="ctitle cs">Where every consolidated interim event lands</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-16-1-14">
            <span>Event</span>
            <span>Statement(s) affected</span>
            <span>Notes</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr cols-16-1-14">
            <span>Consolidated interim statement preparation</span>
            <span>All condensed consolidated statements</span>
            <span>Coordinated with ASBJ Statement No. 37</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s11">
      <span class="num">11</span>
      <h2>Related Standards</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-08-2">
            <span>Standard</span>
            <span>Connection</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr cols-08-2">
            <span>ASBJ Statement No. 37</span>
            <span>The general interim reporting framework this Statement supplements for consolidation purposes</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-08-2">
            <span>ASBJ Statement No. 22</span>
            <span>Supplies the general consolidation principles this Statement adapts for interim reporting</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s12">
      <span class="num">12</span>
      <h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="glossary-item">
          <div class="glossary-term">Consolidated interim financial statements</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">A group's condensed financial statements for an interim period, incorporating subsidiaries' own interim-period data with intercompany eliminations applied.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="legend">
    <div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Japan GAAP terminology)</div>
    <div class="lrow">
      <span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (貸借対照表)
      <span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span> Statement of Income / Profit and Loss Statement (損益計算書)
      <span class="badge bo">Net Assets</span> 純資産の部
      <span class="badge be">SCNA</span> Statement of Changes in Net Assets (株主資本等変動計算書)
      <span class="badge bc">SCF</span> Statement of Cash Flows (キャッシュ・フロー計算書)
    </div>
  </div>

</StandardPageLayout>
